00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:54.900
<i>I don't accept scam phone calls, sorry.</i>

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:58.370
This is no time for jokes! 
Have ya seen the TV?

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:00.120
I'm watching it now.

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:04.710
Your face is blurred out. Makes you
 look like a wanted criminal.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:08.650
<i>Yeah, that occurred to me, too... but...</i>

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:10.180
What's wrong?

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:12.430
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:14.220
It's not your fault.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:17.340
The one to blame is whoever 
posted those photos.

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:21.600
<i>Are you okay?</i>

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:25.460
No problems here. It's <i>him </i>
who's gonna have a hard time.

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:27.350
His family's famous.

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:30.860
Yeah...

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:35.200
<i>Tell him not to get cornered by 
the press and do something dumb.</i>

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.360
How about ya tell him that directly?

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:40.310
<i>I don't know his number.</i>

00:01:40.310 --> 00:01:42.890
<i>I leave it to you, Miss Manager-in-Training.</i>

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:45.870
Sheesh!

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.130
I'm sorry.

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:54.590
I intended to keep LIP×LIP from 
causing the family any trouble.

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:57.330
I apologize for this inci—

00:01:57.330 --> 00:01:58.950
Don't underestimate this family.

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:04.380
The Someyas are not so fragile as 
to be shaken by something like this.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:05.650
Father...

00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:09.290
It seems to me that this 
level of gossip proves

00:02:09.290 --> 00:02:13.160
you've become someone of consequence 
in the entertainment industry.

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:19.170
Yujiro, do you bear any guilt in this?

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:23.530
No. I've done nothing.

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:29.040
Then confront this with the dauntless 
attitude that befits a Someya.

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:30.310
Yes, sir!

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:35.820
<i>No problems here.</i>

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:37.090
Oh, good.

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:38.870
I'm glad.

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:43.860
<i>Tell him not to get careless 
and let the press get a bad photo.</i>

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:47.560
I keep tellin' ya, say that 
stuff to each other <i>directly</i>!

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:49.660
<i>I don't know his number.</i>

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:50.620
<i>Thanks.</i>

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:56.040
Sheesh! Just exchange phone numbers already!

00:02:57.950 --> 00:02:59.800
What'll happen now?

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:05.450
<i>I'm charmed by how you go all-out</i>

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:09.960
<i>I'm charmed by your supportive smile</i>

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:14.340
<i>"I must kiss you," says your Romeo</i>

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:18.300
<i>Glad that you exist and that he met you</i>

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:22.530
<b>Heroines Run the Show</b>

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:29.930
<i>I need more love, want to see you again soon</i>

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:34.020
<i>Lock eyes with you and tell you</i>

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:37.940
<i>My sincerest "Thank you for everything"</i>

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:42.200
<i>Will you love me—
not as a fan, but for real?</i>

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:45.250
<i>"Pick me"</i>

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:48.950
<i>"No, pick me"</i>

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:53.830
<i>Choose which kiss you want</i>

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:57.420
<i>And let your Romeo bind you</i>

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:01.470
<i>I'm charmed by how you go all-out</i>

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:06.010
<i>I'm charmed watching you sing with me</i>

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:09.340
<i>I'm even charmed by your tears</i>

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:13.740
<i>I'm charmed by your supportive smile</i>

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:17.360
<i>Thank you for coming to meet me</i>

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:21.660
<i>Thank you for calling my name</i>

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:26.200
<i>"I must kiss you," says your Romeo</i>

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:30.400
<i>Glad that you exist and that he met you</i>

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:40.750
Well, this has certainly blown up.

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:43.760
Are you all right?

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:46.010
We're perfectly fine.

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:49.600
We don't intend to let 
petty rumors bring us down.

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:53.010
But we apologize for causing 
trouble for the school.

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:54.820
Oh, we anticipated this.

00:04:56.650 --> 00:05:03.150
We accepted you into the school with 
full knowledge that this might happen.

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:04.900
Sir...

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:08.700
Please keep coming to school every day.

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:11.750
Students have the right to learn.

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:15.410
The school will do all it 
can to support that right.

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:16.720
Yes, sir.

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:18.310
Thank you.

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:19.990
We appreciate it.

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:27.880
You go to class. I'll follow later.

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:30.430
Let's avoid talkin' to each 
other at school from now on.

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:34.430
Gotta make sure we don't 
start any more rumors.

00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:36.190
Right...

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:37.160
Understood.

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:48.110
What a pain.

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:52.700
The culprit behind all this is the 
person who posted those photos.

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:56.440
It might be one of our fans here.

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:57.790
Most likely.

00:05:58.390 --> 00:06:01.040
They chose photos where all 
three of us were together,

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:02.960
so I think they have 
something against Suzumi.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:06.980
Jealousy, eh? Which means 
the perp is female.

00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:08.610
This is why I don't like women.

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:11.850
You can have those if you want.

00:06:13.130 --> 00:06:16.770
I know they're crumpled, 
but I think they're good photos.

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:18.570
You look very happy in them.

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:26.370
<i>I thought I was bein' careful. I didn't 
realize how close I was to them.</i>

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:35.770
<i>I gotta keep my distance.</i>

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:39.620
<i>Because I'm the manager-in-trainin'.</i>

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:40.580
This one, please!

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:42.130
<b>School Store</b>

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:42.130
One ham sandwich!

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:46.630
Hey, it's her.

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:50.340
Oh, the one with LIP×LIP. 
Isn't she super plain, though?

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:51.540
Totally.

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:52.460
Not a good match.

00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:55.140
Three bun sandwiches, please!

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:59.560
You bought more buns than usual today.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:01.940
When life gets tough, 
you have another helping!

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:05.810
You seem like you can deal 
with anything, Hiyori.

00:07:05.810 --> 00:07:10.330
It's 'cause I have you and Chizu-chan. 
Thank you, seriously.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:14.200
Are you really not dating either of them?

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:19.380
It's just, you three seemed 
friendly sometimes.

00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:23.580
Aw, come on. There's nothing going on.
 We just sit next to each other.

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:26.340
Really?

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:31.340
I only have eyes for track! 
And I don't know much about idols.

00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:33.090
Okay.

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:39.610
<i>I'm sorry. I can't tell anyone, even my friends.</i>

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:49.520
<i>Look at all the negative comments!</i>

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:54.650
<i>There are plenty of angry fans, 
but so many others seem crushed.</i>

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:57.190
<i>I've...</i>

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:00.680
<i>hurt the fans.</i>

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:07.130
We need to do something to calm the waters.

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:08.680
As a first step,

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:13.230
I've called all their commercial 
sponsors and program producers

00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:15.260
to explain and apologize.

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:17.250
Apologize?! Why?

00:08:17.250 --> 00:08:20.270
We haven't done anything 
we need to apologize for.

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:23.310
Even if you haven't done anything wrong,

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:26.540
it's still potentially damaging to your image.

00:08:26.970 --> 00:08:30.150
We have to apologize for the stir.

00:08:32.910 --> 00:08:36.280
In this business, image is everything.

00:08:37.150 --> 00:08:39.670
Gigs already scheduled are one thing,

00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:43.810
but it's possible that 
you'll lose work in the future.

00:08:45.310 --> 00:08:47.580
I'm sorry! It's my fault.

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:52.290
No, it's not. I made the call to hire you.

00:08:52.870 --> 00:08:56.050
And I'm truly glad that 
I chose you, Hiyori-chan.

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:57.480
Ma'am...

00:08:57.870 --> 00:09:00.180
Why not take a break from school for a while?

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:03.130
No. Isn't that running away?

00:09:03.130 --> 00:09:05.310
I don't approve of hiding.

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:08.970
Nice words, but what if 
something else happens?

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:13.980
Very well. We'll provide support 
so that you can go to school.

00:09:13.980 --> 00:09:17.730
But you're not allowed to go out on 
your own for a while, understood?

00:09:17.730 --> 00:09:19.110
Excuse me.

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:22.600
Someone's here to see Yujiro-san.

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:23.450
Me?

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:28.850
Koichiro...

00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:34.550
Um, you're Someya-kun's 
younger brother, right?

00:09:34.910 --> 00:09:36.700
Is she your girlfriend?

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:38.710
Huh? No!

00:09:38.710 --> 00:09:39.860
That's ludicrous.

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:41.180
I figured.

00:09:43.130 --> 00:09:46.430
If you've got a clean conscience, 
then you should fight back.

00:09:47.030 --> 00:09:52.150
This all started when the photos were 
posted on the school bulletin board.

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:56.060
All of them are photos only 
someone close to you could take.

00:09:56.060 --> 00:09:58.260
It's clearly someone at the school.

00:09:58.770 --> 00:10:01.240
We can trace their online footprints.

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:05.250
And identify who took the photos, eh?

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:08.670
It was probably one of our fans.

00:10:09.490 --> 00:10:11.420
I promise to expose their—

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:13.420
Hold on!

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:17.800
What's the point of suspectin' your 
fans and identifyin' the culprit?!

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:21.050
To give her a stern warning, of course.

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:24.060
You're gonna accuse a fan? That's not good!

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:28.310
Why not? Being a fan doesn't 
justify doing these things.

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:29.140
They need to face—

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:31.810
Fans aren't who idols should be fightin'!

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:35.030
Have ya read your fan letters?!

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:36.320
Do ya know their names?!

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:39.380
They're all lookin' forward 
to what you do next.

00:10:39.380 --> 00:10:44.580
You gotta think of a way to make the 
fans happy, not look for the culprit!

00:10:44.850 --> 00:10:49.080
People have been harassing you, too!
 That doesn't piss you off?

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:52.150
Yeah, it does piss me off!

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:56.090
But more than that, I'm worried 
about LIP×LIP's future.

00:10:57.240 --> 00:10:58.150
Because...

00:10:59.290 --> 00:11:01.590
I'm a fan, too!

00:11:05.340 --> 00:11:09.210
Really, I knew what to do before I got here.

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:15.630
If I made the fans feel bad by 
gettin' too close to LIP×LIP,

00:11:16.090 --> 00:11:18.550
then I've failed my manager trainin'.

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:24.120
So I'm quittin' my manager job!

00:11:25.130 --> 00:11:27.090
Thank you for everything.

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:30.070
I'm home.

00:11:31.380 --> 00:11:33.630
Welcome home!

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:39.380
Wanna have dinner? A bath? 
Or my beautiful body?

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:44.100
You're hungry, right? Food's almost done.

00:11:49.460 --> 00:11:53.480
Looks tasty, right? It's all 
your favorites on parade.

00:11:54.280 --> 00:11:55.230
Why?

00:11:55.580 --> 00:11:58.330
I wanted to cheer up my beloved brother.

00:11:59.810 --> 00:12:00.990
Gross.

00:12:01.730 --> 00:12:04.510
Idols really are popular 
with the chicks, huh?

00:12:05.270 --> 00:12:08.990
I used to be, too, and I fooled 
around with a lot of girls.

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:11.000
You're trash.

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:14.100
Yep, I was trash.

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:18.300
If a girl's feelings got hurt, 
I figured, "Whatever, she had fun, too."

00:12:19.370 --> 00:12:21.480
But you're different.

00:12:21.930 --> 00:12:24.630
Even though you're uncomfortable with girls,

00:12:24.630 --> 00:12:27.380
you still make an effort to talk to 
each one as they crowd around you.

00:12:28.450 --> 00:12:31.430
How about you just say what you're thinking?

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:34.500
I'm sure that'll be the right approach.

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:40.620
And that concludes Your Wonderful 
Brother's Advice Corner.

00:12:40.620 --> 00:12:42.930
"Wonderful Brother," my ass.

00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:45.030
Eat before it gets cold.

00:12:45.550 --> 00:12:47.390
I don't need the reminder!

00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:49.790
Thanks for cooking.

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:02.550
Are you off to training?

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:08.220
Yeah. It throws me off to skip even one day.

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:09.390
Got it.

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:12.560
Thanks for coming to the office tod—

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:13.730
Don't thank me.

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:18.580
I wanted to repay my debt, 
but I wasn't any use.

00:13:18.580 --> 00:13:19.340
Debt?

00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:23.490
That time I hit a wall in my 
training and went to a club,

00:13:24.230 --> 00:13:30.050
you came to stop my senpai from 
forcing me to drink, remember?

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:42.450
You let me get away, and took 
the police lecture in my place.

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:47.470
You didn't tell the police or 
anyone else that it was my fault.

00:13:49.130 --> 00:13:50.220
Why?

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:54.220
Well, why did you call me for help that day?

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:58.410
I-I couldn't tell Father about it...

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:02.230
And I didn't have any friends to ask.

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:03.780
I had to call you.

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:06.620
What choice did I have?!

00:14:06.620 --> 00:14:10.990
I've been in kabuki training my whole life.
 I never got to play with friends!

00:14:11.650 --> 00:14:12.630
I know.

00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:14.860
I've watched you all along.

00:14:15.770 --> 00:14:17.670
And rooted for you, for what it's worth.

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:21.630
You're cute, Koichiro.

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:24.630
What? Are you mocking me?!

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:29.250
Do you still hang out with those senpai?

00:14:29.250 --> 00:14:30.730
Of course not!

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:32.190
That's fine, then.

00:14:32.650 --> 00:14:36.220
You can pay me back later.

00:14:36.590 --> 00:14:38.640
I'll call in the favor when I need it.

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:42.210
Y-You have a terrible personality.

00:14:42.210 --> 00:14:44.350
You're just realizing that now?

00:14:46.670 --> 00:14:49.530
Anyway, was that okay with you?

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:50.910
Was what okay?

00:14:50.910 --> 00:14:52.440
Your manager-in-training leaving.

00:15:00.300 --> 00:15:01.790
You're okay with that?!

00:15:02.430 --> 00:15:05.300
Isn't that dropping out of 
the race halfway through?

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:06.990
Maybe so.

00:15:06.990 --> 00:15:12.510
But I want to support LIP×LIP more 
than I want to keep runnin' my race.

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:16.370
Kiyomi...

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:20.560
<b>Aizo-sama</b>

00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:18.310
Satoe...

00:15:19.250 --> 00:15:20.560
Chutan...

00:15:20.950 --> 00:15:23.940
How about you just say what you're thinking?

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:31.610
<b>Manager-in-Training</b>

00:15:31.610 --> 00:15:31.860
<b>Manager-in-Training</b>

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:33.620
<b>Manager-in-Training</b>

00:15:38.150 --> 00:15:41.600
<i>This is Uchida at Möbius. I can't 
come to the phone right now, so—</i>

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:43.630
Damn it, what a pain!

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:50.630
Weren't you going to make 
us admit your worth?

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:57.670
Yeah, but right now reassuring the 
fans is more important than my goals.

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:04.150
What's wrong, Hotaru?

00:16:04.780 --> 00:16:05.780
Yo.

00:16:05.780 --> 00:16:06.790
A monkey?

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:07.820
Hey!

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:14.400
What are you doing here? And so late?

00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:16.410
Everything about this is wrong.

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:18.540
How else could I contact you?

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:23.920
Uchida-san isn't answering her phone, 
and the manager-in-training quit.

00:16:24.180 --> 00:16:27.670
If someone sees you, they'll call 
the police on you for trespassing.

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:30.150
Someone already saw me. A maid.

00:16:30.150 --> 00:16:30.840
Huh?

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:34.180
She let me in when she heard my name. 
The story is that we're "friends."

00:16:34.790 --> 00:16:36.800
"Friends," eh?

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:39.430
Wanna exchange phone numbers, like friends do?

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:40.930
No.

00:16:40.930 --> 00:16:42.930
Nope, me either.

00:16:43.640 --> 00:16:46.690
I'm not letting you in. 
Because we're not friends.

00:16:47.040 --> 00:16:50.610
I wouldn't come in if you told 
me to. We're not friends.

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:53.330
So what do you want?

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:56.450
I have a proposal.

00:16:59.950 --> 00:17:03.990
No work to go to... I'm goin' back to sleep.

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:10.460
Oh, it's Uchida-san.

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:14.970
"LIP×LIP will hold a press 
conference today at 3 PM"?!

00:17:18.660 --> 00:17:23.560
Which of you is dating 
the girl in the photos?

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:27.230
Neither of us has a girlfriend.

00:17:27.800 --> 00:17:32.320
Exactly. Because we have many 
fans—Julietas—supporting us.

00:17:32.630 --> 00:17:36.040
Then what is your relationship 
with the girl in the photos?

00:17:36.040 --> 00:17:38.320
You look very friendly in them.

00:17:38.540 --> 00:17:42.390
We are friendly. She's one 
of our precious classmates.

00:17:42.390 --> 00:17:46.280
"Precious" makes it sound 
like she's special to you.

00:17:46.280 --> 00:17:50.400
She sits near us, so there are lots of 
opportunities to interact, that's all.

00:17:50.400 --> 00:17:52.840
We also ran the relay together on Field Day.

00:17:53.060 --> 00:17:55.690
I see. So you participate 
in the school's events.

00:17:55.690 --> 00:17:58.840
Why did you enter a normal high school 
despite having so many job offers?

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:02.510
Because we're high school idols.

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:05.850
The truth is, though, we didn't 
intend to go to high school.

00:18:06.280 --> 00:18:07.160
Oh?

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:09.500
We debuted in our third year of middle school,

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:13.300
so this was a year when we 
needed to work hard as idols.

00:18:13.300 --> 00:18:16.520
We wanted to give our 
time to work and lessons.

00:18:16.520 --> 00:18:17.860
What changed your minds?

00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:20.260
The CEO of our agency told us

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:24.610
she wanted us to enjoy high school life, 
because that chance only comes once.

00:18:24.610 --> 00:18:26.120
We bowed to her wishes.

00:18:26.890 --> 00:18:30.730
To be honest, I wasn't 
very motivated at first.

00:18:30.730 --> 00:18:35.050
But lately, I'm starting to 
understand what she meant.

00:18:35.050 --> 00:18:39.130
We got invited to play basketball 
during recess the other day.

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:41.750
It was surprisingly fun.

00:18:42.090 --> 00:18:45.140
So much fun I forgot I was
 an idol for a moment.

00:18:45.630 --> 00:18:50.170
We go to class with our classmates, 
we talk about trivial things,

00:18:50.490 --> 00:18:52.170
and we eat lunch together.

00:18:53.340 --> 00:18:57.710
Those little day-to-day things 
feel precious to me now.

00:18:59.980 --> 00:19:01.400
The girl in those photos

00:19:01.400 --> 00:19:06.160
is one of the classmates living 
high school life with us.

00:19:06.900 --> 00:19:09.830
She didn't even know we were idols at first.

00:19:10.150 --> 00:19:13.170
She's a hard worker who loves 
her after-school activities.

00:19:13.510 --> 00:19:17.180
She happens to be in our class, 
and because she sits near us,

00:19:17.650 --> 00:19:21.180
she's been a little closer 
to us than the others.

00:19:22.620 --> 00:19:26.760
We feel terrible that she's been 
dragged into this drama because of that.

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:33.260
Our agency actually suggested we 
stop going to school for a while

00:19:33.260 --> 00:19:35.230
because of the media circus.

00:19:35.880 --> 00:19:38.390
We might have been happy to do that before.

00:19:39.190 --> 00:19:40.490
But now...

00:19:41.030 --> 00:19:45.740
If we can, we'd like to 
keep attending high school.

00:19:46.390 --> 00:19:48.990
So we hope you'll watch over us.

00:19:49.530 --> 00:19:50.730
Thank you.

00:19:56.390 --> 00:19:58.460
Since the press conference aired,

00:19:58.460 --> 00:20:02.510
more and more people are expressing 
support for their high school life.

00:20:02.980 --> 00:20:07.850
They've received a lot of encouragement 
from business partners, too.

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:10.520
<i>How's the fan response?</i>

00:20:10.520 --> 00:20:14.020
Just fine. In fact, they gained new fans!

00:20:14.020 --> 00:20:15.900
Oh, good!

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:18.780
Thank you for callin' to tell me.

00:20:19.160 --> 00:20:21.480
<i>Hiyoko, thank you.</i>

00:20:22.790 --> 00:20:28.750
I think they've managed to come 
this far as high school idols

00:20:24.030 --> 00:20:31.540
<i>"Julieta" Concert Tour
<b></b></i>New Date Added

00:20:28.750 --> 00:20:31.540
because you were with them.

00:20:31.780 --> 00:20:34.150
<i>Thank you, truly.</i>

00:20:35.390 --> 00:20:42.180
I'm sorry I didn't finish 
my trainin', Uchida-san.

00:20:42.180 --> 00:20:44.270
Thank you for everything.

00:20:44.740 --> 00:20:47.350
<i>I wish you well in track, Hiyoko.</i>

00:20:48.130 --> 00:20:52.100
Thanks! Goodbye.

00:20:57.400 --> 00:21:01.150
It was rough pretty much every day, huh?

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:04.580
Our meeting was a disaster.

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:07.580
And I landed the manager-in-training job,

00:21:07.580 --> 00:21:10.120
but they were always fightin'!

00:21:11.090 --> 00:21:14.330
But they defended me at their shoot.

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:18.290
And I watched their show 
from the good seats.

00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:23.510
And they produced me that time...

00:21:25.380 --> 00:21:27.260
And we ran the relay together...

00:21:30.990 --> 00:21:32.760
It was fun.

00:21:37.620 --> 00:21:41.860
<i>I wish I coulda stayed in that job.</i>

00:21:43.230 --> 00:21:45.240
<b>EMERGENCY PRESS CONFERENCE ABOUT LIP×LIP'S REPORTED AFFAIR</b>

00:21:50.990 --> 00:21:55.000
<b>Episode 10</b>

00:21:50.990 --> 00:21:55.000
<b>I'm Quittin' My Manager Job!</b>

00:22:06.010 --> 00:22:09.830
<i>The whole neighborhood is one color</i>

00:22:10.350 --> 00:22:16.100
<i>Different colors just got pointed at</i>

00:22:16.100 --> 00:22:19.790
<i>So they hid away, afraid</i>

00:22:20.450 --> 00:22:26.740
<i>And started becoming that same color</i>

00:22:26.740 --> 00:22:29.500
<i>Tomorrow</i>

00:22:27.340 --> 00:22:29.740
<i>Don't run from what you love</i>

00:22:29.740 --> 00:22:32.360
<i>Hold your head high and shine</i>

00:22:32.360 --> 00:22:36.750
<i>It's a big world! Look and see</i>

00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:39.230
<i>We...</i>

00:22:37.460 --> 00:22:39.870
<i>Learn to be selfish</i>

00:22:39.870 --> 00:22:42.610
<i>Stick with our dreams, not our peers</i>

00:22:42.610 --> 00:22:47.710
<i>That negative self? Leave it behind</i>

00:22:48.300 --> 00:22:54.010
<i>Your hue is beautiful and one of a kind</i>

00:22:54.010 --> 00:22:58.940
<i>Like a flower giving the world color</i>

00:22:58.940 --> 00:23:05.860
<i>Come on, lift your head, no need to be shy</i>

00:23:05.860 --> 00:23:08.950
<i>Stay your special self</i>

00:23:09.300 --> 00:23:14.200
<i>Isn't it a waste not to do 
what you want? Athlete's oath</i>

00:23:14.200 --> 00:23:19.210
<i>Another person's dream 
won't do! Enjoy yourself</i>

00:23:19.210 --> 00:23:25.000
<i>For doing your best, we dedicate 
this dream fanfare to you</i>

00:23:26.270 --> 00:23:33.070
Next time, on episode 11 of 
<i>Heroines Run the Show</i>...

00:23:33.070 --> 00:23:35.010
"Battle of the Hated Heroine"!

00:23:34.200 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Episode 11
Battle of the Hated Heroine</b>
